sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant WA as Meta Cloud API
    participant CE as Conversation Engine
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    Note over C,DB: Entry via the webhook gate (previous figure). session.state = cart_review:<br/>the customer has the summary with items, delivery fee and total.<br/>While orders are paused (FR-28) the gate answers with the paused text first, so no order is written.
    C->>WA: sends the confirm word
    WA->>CE: webhook
    CE->>DB: SELECT the session FOR UPDATE
    CE->>DB: SELECT is_available, category is_active FOR every cart line
    DB-->>CE: current availability (prices are not re-read: a line keeps its price)
    alt some lines unavailable
        CE->>WA: name the removed lines and send a new summary<br/>(back to browsing if none is left)
        WA->>C: delivered
    else every line available
        CE->>DB: UPDATE conversation_sessions SET state='order_placed'<br/>WHERE id=? AND state='cart_review'
        DB-->>CE: rowcount
        alt rowcount = 0 (duplicate confirm)
            Note over CE,DB: No second order. This is the compare-and-swap layer.
        else rowcount = 1
            CE->>DB: pg_advisory_xact_lock(restaurant) · next order number (MAX + 1, from 101)
            CE->>DB: INSERT orders (cash, pending_cash, pending_acceptance,<br/>delivery fee and address, notified=true, outbound_msg_count)
            DB-->>CE: order.id
            CE->>DB: INSERT order_items (name and unit price snapshotted)
            CE->>DB: INSERT order_status_history (NULL to pending_acceptance, actor='customer')
            CE->>DB: COMMIT
            CE->>WA: "we received your order no. N" — only after the commit
            WA->>C: delivered
        end
    end
